# Phase 3c vendor bundle — the exceptions to "never commit .js".
# These two are NOT tsc output and have no .ts sibling:
#   scripts/build-vendor.js is a hand-written build tool (like download-geo.ts's
#   role, but plain Node — it must run before any TypeScript build exists), and
#   renderer/hub/vendor/vgplot.js is its committed output. Committing the bundle
#   is what keeps CI and electron-builder off the 180+ MB vgplot tree.
!/scripts/build-vendor.js
!/renderer/hub/vendor/vgplot.js

# scripts/build-icons.js — same exception, same reason: a hand-written build
# tool with no .ts sibling. It bakes assets/provider-icons.json so simple-icons
# can be a devDependency instead of 25 MB of runtime dependency.
!/scripts/build-icons.js

# Phase 3c Mosaic connector (mosaic:view / mosaic:query) — emitted siblings.
